      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`--speculative-num-draft-tokens` may override the DSpark checkpoint block size. The worker and folded proposer honor the runtime gamma, but `DeepseekV4ForCausalLMDSpark.compute_confidence()` reshaped the confidence tap with the checkpoint's `self.gamma`.\n\nWhen checkpoint and runtime gamma differ, folded graph capture can therefore apply an incompatible confidence shape.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Derive confidence geometry from the live `sampled_tokens` shape.\n- Use the live gamma when constructing Markov-history features.\n- Validate sampled-token and hidden-row geometry with actionable errors.\n- Preserve view semantics for graph capture.\n- Add a CPU regression covering a runtime gamma override.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Runtime-override confidence output shape.\n- Markov predecessor-token construction.\n- Explicit rejection of mismatched hidden-row geometry.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo behavior or cost change is expected when runtime gamma equals checkpoint gamma. No public performance claim is made in this PR.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format changed code with Ruff.\n- [x] Add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation if required.\n",
